solve The Three Gods
Three gods, A, B, and C, are called True, False, and Random, in some unknown order. True always speaks truly, False always speaks falsely, and Random's answers are completely random: each time, he flips a coin in his head to decide whether to lie or tell the truth.
Your task is to figure out which god is which by asking three yes-or-no questions. Each question goes to exactly one god, and you may ask the same god more than one question. What you ask later can depend on the answers you got earlier.
The catch is that the gods understand your language but always answer in their own. Their words for yes and no are "da" and "ja", and you don't know which word means which.
Which three questions do you ask?
Take your time with it. When you want one, I can give you a hint, a bigger nudge, or the full solution. And if you'd rather have a different kind of riddle (fewer moving parts but still tricky, or something math-flavored), just say so.



